vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}].$ Multiplying by the matrix $T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x-y+4z \\\\ 5x+3y-2z \\\\ x-6y+7z\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\,T\\,$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2x-y+4z \\\\ 5x+3y-2z \\\\ x-6y+7z\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005887/state.json" "file_sha256" "090e738f3f3eea9e0899b6b755238681a79e55e772ac00dfb3edc424fb6740e9"} {"question" "q-317044" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c3d9df000b8d04304601ba1ed0194385592924551b158acc1ccd751b48fece3e"} {"question" "q-317044" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005887/state.json" "file_sha256" "090e738f3f3eea9e0899b6b755238681a79e55e772ac00dfb3edc424fb6740e9"} {"question" "q-317044" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x-y+4z"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005887/state.json" "file_sha256" "090e738f3f3eea9e0899b6b755238681a79e55e772ac00dfb3edc424fb6740e9"} {"question" "q-317044" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14